From 8378380e667630f824764fce452a5c484e94c130 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TimmyTurner51 <timmy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 22:17:07 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] FEXCore/Windows: per-block invalidation under SMCChecks=full

Under full SMC every block compiled from writable code validates its own
bytes on entry, so a code change only needs to drop the affected block
instead of its whole page. Adds single-block invalidation paths
(InvalidateCodeBuffersBlock/InvalidateThreadCachedBlock) and stops
write-trapping RWX pages when full SMC already covers them. Also recovers
executable VMAs that a protect-split dropped from the tracker.
